`__gt__(self, other)` defines the `>` operator. Return `True` or `False`, or `NotImplemented` if the other type is unsupported so Python can try the reflected operation. With `functools.total_ordering`, defining `__eq__` and one comparison fills in the rest.

```python
from functools import total_ordering


@total_ordering
class Version:
    def __init__(self, n):
        self.n = n

    def __eq__(self, other):
        return self.n == other.n

    def __gt__(self, other):
        return self.n > other.n


print(Version(3) > Version(2))   # True
print(Version(3) <= Version(2))  # False (from total_ordering)
```

